      "status": "studied",
      "studiedAt": "2026-09-02T11:23:08.208Z",
      "studiedNote": "990 Beckett taught that a project can use every standard AOI and still be an anti-pattern: the failures are structural — many state machines per program, hand-indexed alarms instead of the alarm handler, AlwaysOff-driven state selection, cross-machine Control writes, index-as-meaning HMI arrays, and triplicated production counters — plus new legacy device evidence (Telesis mark/verify protocol, controller CF recipe file engine, Kinetix 5100 non-group axis).",
      "sizeBytes": 7345338,
      "hash": "250f5f91715e",
      "priority": 110
