      "studiedNote": "The ProgramAlarmHandler AOI interface taught the exact division of labor between a station alarm rung (Active/Severity/Message) and the handler (ProgramID, DT timestamp from the CPU clock UDT, Count/Duration, publishing to p_Active and history, HMI_ResetCount), plus that AlarmData's flag bits are packed in a hidden SINT so entries move atomically under COP.",
      "sizeBytes": 25711,
      "hash": "f2fd446d477e",
      "priority": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "ci_54554a6a8667",
      "path": "plc-reference/standards-docs/Standards - Software/Allen Bradley/Programs/AOI's/Alarm Handler/ProgramAlarmHandler.L5X",
      "kind": "standard-program",
      "topics": [
        "alarms"
      ],
      "antiPattern": false,
      "conceptFiles": [
        "alarms.md"
      ],
      "status": "studied",
      "studiedAt": "2026-09-16T11:22:12.492Z",
      "studiedNote": "The alarm handler AOI's own parameter list names the fault output AlarmActiveTag (not FaultActiveTag) and stamps TimeStamp as a LINT of UTC microseconds from the CPU_TimeDate UDT, with STRING100 capping composed messages at 100 characters.",
      "sizeBytes": 23715,
      "hash": "38e1ffc99eb7",
      "priority": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "ci_8f9393e5b8e3",
      "path": "plc-reference/standards-docs/Standards - Software/Allen Bradley/Programs/AOI's/Top Alarms/TopAlarms.L5X",
